# Hide spam authors with HIDDEN_AUTHOR_PUBKEYS

When asked to ban, block, or hide a pubkey from the trending feed, **append it to the existing `HIDDEN_AUTHOR_PUBKEYS` sets**. Do not invent a new block list, and do not use Settings mutes (`mutedAuthors`) for global bans.

## Required (keep both in sync)

```ts
// src/nostr.ts
const HIDDEN_AUTHOR_PUBKEYS = new Set([/* ... */, "lowercase-hex-pubkey"]);

// lib/trendingFeed.js  (server trending blob — same keys)
const HIDDEN_AUTHOR_PUBKEYS = new Set([/* ... */, "lowercase-hex-pubkey"]);
```

Lowercase hex only. Applied in `toLocatedEvents` before ranking.

## Do not

- Add `BLOCKED_PUBKEYS` (or similar) in `identity.ts` — that file is for nip-05 hosts / display names only
- Mute via `muteAuthor` / Settings for a site-wide ban
- Update only one of `src/nostr.ts` or `lib/trendingFeed.js`
